IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble (applies to every query below): assume every condition
-- and exclusion NOT referenced in the question is satisfied / not triggered.
-- Also assume, per the paper's prompts, that the agreement has been signed
-- and the premium has been paid on time. Baseline "unrelated" defaults used
-- throughout: agreement signed; premium paid at month 0; wellness visit at
-- month 3 with a qualified provider, confirmed at month 5 (both comfortably
-- inside the 6- and 7-month deadlines); no fraud, misrepresentation, or
-- dispute; policy term of 12 months (one year, per Section 3.6.1).

§ `Q1 -- firefighter, burns suffered on duty`

q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                    IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                  IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`               IS 5
    `hospitalization ground`              IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`              IS 40
    `causes`                              IS LIST Firefighting
    `fraud month`                         IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`             IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                IS JUST 3
    `wellness visit provider qualified`   IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`          IS JUST 5
    `dispute arisen`                      IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`              IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`         IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`      IS FALSE
    `written proof of claim month`        IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`               IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                  IS 12

#EVAL covered q1

